# Architecture

## Crate naming

Rust crates in `codex-rs/` are prefixed `codex-`. Directory `foo` → crate `codex-foo`. Utils: `codex-rs/utils/<name>` → `codex-utils-<name>`.

## Key crates

- `cli` — entry point, CLAP, subcommand dispatch
- `tui` — ratatui interactive UI
- `exec` — non-interactive execution
- `app-server` (+ protocol, client, daemon) — JSON-RPC for IDE integrations
- `exec-server` — WebSocket exec server
- `mcp-server` — MCP stdio server
- `core` — config, agent loop, context, tool routing (**avoid adding code here**)
- `config`, `protocol`, `login`, `backend-client`, `codex-mcp`
- `model-provider`, `models-manager`, `execpolicy`
- `sandboxing`, `connectors`, `file-search`, `hooks`, `plugin`, `state`
- `ext/` — image-generation, web-search, memories, goal, guardian

## Entry point

`codex-rs/cli/src/main.rs` — `MultitoolCli`, ~25 subcommands, `bin_name = "sakrylle"`. No subcommand → interactive TUI.

## Auth (`codex-rs/login/`)

- ChatGPT OAuth (default interactive)
- API key (`--with-api-key`, stdin)
- Access token (`--with-access-token`, stdin)
- Device code OIDC (`--device-auth`)
- Agent JWT (`CODEX_ACCESS_TOKEN`)

Sakrylle fork: OIDC auto-login and arrow-key login prompts on first run.
